slug: mmt-grading-0-to-5
title: Manual Muscle Testing — The 0 to 5 Scale Without Guesswork
area: Skills · Measurement
level: Foundation
best: 1st year onwards
minutes: 13
hook: Grade 3 is the line between a muscle that can lift the limb and one that cannot. Learn the scale, the gravity-decides rule and how to resist without guessing. || Grade 3 us muscle ke beech ki line hai jo limb ko utha sakta hai aur jo nahi utha sakta. Scale, gravity-decides ka qaida aur bina andaza lagaye resist karna seekhein.
goal: By the end, you'll grade strength 0–5 for any muscle, choose the correct gravity position, give resistance at the right place and time, and record the result clearly. || End tak aap kisi bhi muscle ki taqat 0–5 grade karenge, sahi gravity position chunenge, sahi jagah aur sahi waqt par resistance denge aur result saaf likhenge.

say: MMT grades a muscle's strength by what it can do **against gravity and against your hand**. **0** no contraction; **1** a flicker or palpable tension but no movement; **2** moves through the full range with **gravity eliminated**; **3** moves through the full range **against gravity**; **4** holds against gravity plus **moderate** resistance; **5** holds against **maximal** resistance (normal). Grade 3 is the pivot: below it the muscle cannot beat gravity, above it it adds resistance. || MMT muscle ki taqat is se grade karta hai ke woh **gravity aur aap ke haath ke khilaf** kya kar sakta hai. **0** koi contraction nahi; **1** halki harkat ya mehsoos hone wala tanao lekin movement nahi; **2** **gravity hata kar** poori range mein move; **3** **gravity ke khilaf** poori range mein move; **4** gravity ke saath **moderate** resistance ke khilaf hold; **5** **maximal** resistance ke khilaf hold (normal). Grade 3 pivot hai: iske neeche muscle gravity ko nahi hara sakta, iske upar resistance bhi jorta hai.
analogy: Strength grades are like lifting a shopping bag. Grade 0–2 cannot lift it at all (you slide it along a table instead — gravity removed). Grade 3 lifts it off the table. Grade 4 lifts it while someone presses down moderately. Grade 5 lifts it even while a strong person pushes hard. || Taqat ke grades shopping bag uthane jaise hain. Grade 0–2 usay uthaa hi nahi sakta (iske bajaye aap mez par sarka dete hain — gravity hat gayi). Grade 3 usay mez se uthata hai. Grade 4 tab uthata hai jab koi moderate dabaye. Grade 5 tab bhi uthata hai jab koi mazboot shakhs zor se dhakele.
demo: manual-muscle-testing/concept:gravity-decides :: Gravity decides the first step :: Watch how the test starts: the patient moves the limb **against gravity** first. If they can complete the range, you test grade 4 and 5 by adding resistance. If not, you move to the gravity-minimised position for grades 2, 1 and 0. || Dekhein test kaise shuru hota hai: patient pehle limb ko **gravity ke khilaf** move karta hai. Agar range poori kar le to aap resistance laga kar grade 4 aur 5 test karte hain. Agar nahi, to grade 2, 1 aur 0 ke liye gravity-minimised position par jate hain.
check: A patient cannot lift the arm against gravity but can move it fully when it rests on a smooth board. What is the grade? || Patient arm ko gravity ke khilaf nahi utha sakta lekin smooth board par rakha ho to poori range mein move kar leta hai. Grade kya hai?
ok: Grade 2 || Grade 2 || Yes — full range with gravity eliminated is grade 2. Grade 3 needs full range against gravity. || Haan — gravity hata kar poori range grade 2 hai. Grade 3 ke liye gravity ke khilaf poori range chahiye.
no: Grade 3 || Grade 3 || Grade 3 means he can complete the range against gravity. || Grade 3 ka matlab hai woh gravity ke khilaf range poori kar sakta hai.
no: Grade 1 || Grade 1 || Grade 1 means only a flicker, with no movement. || Grade 1 ka matlab sirf halki harkat, movement nahi.
steps: The universal 8-step test || Aathh steps ka universal test
step: Explain and get consent :: Say what you will do and ask about pain before you start. || Samjhayein aur consent lein :: Kya karenge batayein aur shuru karne se pehle dard ke baare mein poochein.
step: Position (against gravity first) :: Use the standard position for the muscle so you can grade it reliably. || Position (pehle gravity ke khilaf) :: Muscle ki standard position use karein taake aap reliably grade de saken.
step: Stabilise the proximal segment :: Hold the part the muscle originates from so the patient cannot cheat with the trunk or neighbouring joints. || Proximal segment ko stabilise karein :: Woh hissa pakrein jahan se muscle shuru hota hai taake patient trunk ya qareeb ke joints se cheat na kar sake.
step: Show the movement :: Move the part passively through range to demonstrate and to check the range is available. || Movement dikhayein :: Hissay ko passively range mein move kar ke dikhayein aur check karein ke range maujood hai.
step: Test grade 3, then resist :: Ask the patient to move against gravity; if they complete it, build resistance over 2–3 seconds at the **distal** end of the moving segment. || Grade 3 test karein, phir resist :: Patient se gravity ke khilaf move karwayein; agar poori kar le to moving segment ke **distal** end par 2–3 seconds mein resistance barhayein.
step: Grade and compare sides :: Decide 4 or 5 (or 3 if resistance breaks the position instantly) and test the other side. || Grade dein aur sides compare karein :: 4 ya 5 tay karein (ya agar resistance position foran tor de to 3) aur doosri side test karein.
step: Document :: Side, movement or muscle, grade, pain and any substitution. || Document karein :: Side, movement ya muscle, grade, dard aur koi substitution.
demo: manual-muscle-testing/elbow-flexion :: Elbow flexion — make the test visible :: Watch the elbow bend against gravity with the forearm supinated, then the examiner **resists at the distal forearm** (near the wrist) while the other hand stabilises the upper arm. The "You say" line shows the instruction to give. || Dekhein elbow gravity ke khilaf mud'ta hai (forearm supinated), phir examiner **distal forearm par** (kalai ke qareeb) resist karta hai aur doosra haath upper arm ko stabilise karta hai. “You say” line instruction dikhati hai.
mistake: **Pushing in the wrong place or too suddenly.** Resistance should be at the **distal end** of the moving segment (the lever is longest there) and build **slowly**, not a jab. A sudden push tests the patient's reflexes, not their strength; resisting at the mid-segment makes a weak muscle look strong. Another trap is grading 5 because the patient "feels strong": compare sides and remember that a normal for a small patient is not the same as a normal for a large examiner. || **Ghalat jagah ya achanak dhakka.** Resistance moving segment ke **distal end** par ho (lever wahan sab se lamba hai) aur **aahista** barhe, jhatka nahi. Achanak dhakka patient ke reflexes test karta hai, taqat nahi; mid-segment par resist karne se kamzor muscle mazboot lagta hai. Ek aur jaal: patient “mazboot mehsoos karta hai” to grade 5 dena: sides compare karein aur yaad rakhein ke chhote patient ka normal bade examiner ke normal jaisa nahi.
check: Where should you apply resistance when testing a muscle? || Muscle test karte waqt resistance kahan lagayein?
ok: At the distal end of the segment that the muscle moves, building slowly over 2–3 seconds || Us segment ke distal end par jise muscle hilata hai, 2–3 seconds mein aahista barhate hue || Yes — the distal end gives the longest lever, so the force is graded and reproducible. || Haan — distal end sab se lamba lever deta hai, is liye force grade aur dobara kiya ja sakta hai.
no: In the middle of the segment, with a quick push || Segment ke beech mein, tez dhakke se || A quick push in the middle gives unreliable grades. || Beech mein tez dhakka bharosay ke qabil grades nahi deta.
no: Over the joint that is moving || Jo joint hil raha hai uske upar || Resisting over the joint does not load the muscle through its lever. || Joint ke upar resist karne se muscle lever ke zariye load nahi hota.
demo: manual-muscle-testing/knee-extension :: Knee extension — a big muscle :: The quadriceps is very strong. You will often grade it 4 when the patient could still hold much more: that is why a handheld dynamometer or a single-leg sit-to-stand is better for strong patients. || Quadriceps bohat mazboot hai. Aap aksar isay 4 grade karenge jab ke patient abhi bahut zyada pakar sakta hai: isi liye mazboot patients ke liye handheld dynamometer ya single-leg sit-to-stand behtar hai.
clinic: **Document like a professional.** "R shoulder abduction 4/5, pain at end range; L 5/5. Break test, sitting." A two-column table (right and left) lets anyone see the pattern at a glance. Use the same method (make or break) and position every time, and for weakness that matters for function (sport, work), add a dynamometer or a functional test such as 30-second sit-to-stand, single-leg heel raises or the hop test. || **Professional tareeqay se document karein.** “R shoulder abduction 4/5, end range par dard; L 5/5. Break test, sitting.” Do-column table (right aur left) kisi ko bhi ek nazar mein pattern dikha deta hai. Har baar wohi method (make ya break) aur position use karein, aur function ke liye ahem kamzori (sport, kaam) mein dynamometer ya functional test jaise 30-second sit-to-stand, single-leg heel raises ya hop test jorein.
evidence: Reliability of MMT is **good for grades 0–3 but poor between grades 4 and 5**: a strong examiner cannot "break" a strong patient, so moderate weakness hides at grade 5, and in muscles like the quadriceps and calf manual testing misses up to a half of the true strength deficit. Handheld dynamometry is more sensitive and reproducible. MMT is also invalid in spasticity, because voluntary isolated control is missing. || MMT ki reliability **grades 0–3 mein achi lekin 4 aur 5 ke beech kamzor** hai: mazboot examiner mazboot patient ko “tor” nahi sakta, is liye moderate kamzori grade 5 mein chhup jati hai, aur quadriceps aur calf jaise muscles mein manual testing asal taqat ki kami ka aadha tak chhor deti hai. Handheld dynamometry zyada sensitive aur reproducible hai. Spasticity mein MMT valid nahi, kyunke voluntary isolated control maujood nahi.
reveal: A patient with a stroke has a stiff, spastic arm. Should you grade the biceps 0–5 with MMT? || Stroke ke patient ka arm sakht aur spastic hai. Kya biceps ko MMT se 0–5 grade karna chahiye? || Usually not. MMT assumes selective voluntary control and no abnormal tone; in spasticity, strength and tone interact and a "weak" muscle may be limited by co-contraction. Describe tone (Ashworth/Tardieu), selective motor control and function instead. || Aam taur par nahi. MMT maanta hai ke selective voluntary control hai aur ghair-mamooli tone nahi; spasticity mein taqat aur tone ek doosre ko mutasir karte hain aur “kamzor” muscle co-contraction se limit ho sakta hai. Iske bajaye tone (Ashworth/Tardieu), selective motor control aur function describe karein.
check: Which grade can a handheld dynamometer help you separate that MMT often cannot? || Handheld dynamometer kaun si grades ko alag karne mein madad deta hai jo MMT aksar nahi kar pata?
ok: 4 versus 5 (mild to moderate deficits hidden at "normal") || 4 vs 5 (halki se moderate kami jo “normal” mein chhup jati hai) || Yes — it measures force in kilograms or newtons, so smaller differences and change over time become visible. || Haan — yeh force kilograms ya newtons mein naapta hai, is liye chhote farq aur waqt ke saath tabdeeli nazar aati hai.
no: 0 versus 1 || 0 vs 1 || Palpation separates these; no device is needed. || Palpation inhein alag karti hai; device ki zaroorat nahi.
no: 2 versus 3 || 2 vs 3 || Gravity separates these. || Gravity inhein alag karti hai.
safety: **Do not resist** over an unhealed fracture, recent surgery (follow the protocol), acute inflammation or a suspected tear. Teach the patient to breathe out during effort: a long hold with held breath (Valsalva) raises blood pressure, which is risky in cardiac disease and hypertension. Stop if the test reproduces significant pain, and be gentle with osteoporosis. || **Resist na karein** unhealed fracture, haali surgery (protocol follow karein), acute inflammation ya shak-e-tear par. Patient ko effort ke dauran saans bahar nikalna sikhayein: saans roke hue lambi hold (Valsalva) blood pressure barhati hai jo cardiac bimari aur hypertension mein khatarnak hai. Agar test se kaafi dard ho to ruk jayein, aur osteoporosis mein halka rahein.
summary: 0 none, 1 flicker, 2 full range gravity-eliminated, 3 full range against gravity, 4 against moderate resistance, 5 against maximal resistance. || 0 koi nahi, 1 halki harkat, 2 gravity hata kar poori range, 3 gravity ke khilaf poori range, 4 moderate resistance ke khilaf, 5 maximal resistance ke khilaf.
summary: Use the 8 steps: explain, position, stabilise, show, test grade 3 then resist slowly at the distal end, grade and compare, document. || 8 steps use karein: samjhayein, position, stabilise, dikhayein, grade 3 test phir distal end par aahista resist, grade aur compare, document.
summary: MMT is reliable for 0–3 but weak between 4 and 5; use dynamometry or functional tests for strong patients and do not use MMT in spasticity. || MMT 0–3 ke liye reliable lekin 4 aur 5 ke beech kamzor hai; mazboot patients ke liye dynamometry ya functional tests use karein aur spasticity mein MMT use na karein.
card: Define MMT grades 2 and 3. || MMT grades 2 aur 3 define karein. || Grade 2: full range with gravity eliminated. Grade 3: full range against gravity. || Grade 2: gravity hata kar poori range. Grade 3: gravity ke khilaf poori range.
card: Where do you apply resistance? || Resistance kahan lagate hain? || At the distal end of the segment the muscle moves, building slowly over 2–3 seconds. || Us segment ke distal end par jise muscle hilata hai, 2–3 seconds mein aahista barhate hue.
card: What is the weak spot of MMT? || MMT ki kamzori kya hai? || Poor discrimination between grades 4 and 5 and in large strong muscles; use a dynamometer. || Grades 4 aur 5 ke beech aur bare mazboot muscles mein kamzor farq; dynamometer use karein.
card: When is MMT the wrong tool? || MMT kab ghalat tool hai? || In spasticity, in young children, severe pain or cognitive impairment; use tone, function and observation instead. || Spasticity, chhote bachon, shadeed dard ya cognitive impairment mein; iske bajaye tone, function aur observation use karein.
deeper: Manual muscle testing skill in the Skills Lab || /skills/manual-muscle-testing || Test 44 muscles in 3D with the examiner's hands and the instruction to give. || 44 muscles 3D mein test karein, examiner ke haath aur dene wali instruction ke saath.
deeper: Muscle contraction types lesson || /learn/muscle-contraction-types || Understand isometric, concentric and eccentric muscle work. || Isometric, concentric aur eccentric muscle work samjhein.
source: Cuthbert SC, Goodheart GJ Jr. On the reliability and validity of manual muscle testing: a literature review. Chiropr Osteopat. 2007;15:4. || manual muscle testing reliability validity review
source: Bohannon RW. Manual muscle testing: does it meet the standards of an adequate screening test? Clin Rehabil. 2005;19:662–667. || manual muscle testing screening test standards
